    {q:"Under Utah's health benefit plan information card law, all of the following must appear on the card EXCEPT:", c:["The covered person's name","The carrier and network name","Whether the plan is regulated by the state","The premium amount"], a:3, w:"31A-22-636 requires name, carrier and network, contact information, copay and deductible information, and a state-regulation indicator. The premium isn't on the card.", o:"11.8", ut:true},
    {q:"Under Utah law, which of these must issue a standardized health benefit plan information card to its enrollees?", c:["Only HMOs","Insurers, HMOs and third party administrators","Only licensed A&H insurers","Only plans sold on the federal exchange"], a:1, w:"31A-22-636 defines 'insurer' broadly for the card: A&H insurers, HMOs, third party administrators and PEHP health plans, upon purchase, renewal or enrollment.", o:"11.8", ut:true},
    {q:"Under the ACA, a gold plan is designed to pay, on average, what percentage of covered health care costs?", c:["60%","70%","80%","90%"], a:2, w:"Bronze 60, silver 70, gold 80, platinum 90. It's an average (actuarial value), not the coinsurance on each claim.", o:"11.9", ut:false},
    {q:"Under the ACA, individual health insurance premiums may vary by all of the following EXCEPT:", c:["Age","Tobacco use","Geographic area","Health status"], a:3, w:"ACA rating allows age (up to 3:1), tobacco (up to 1.5:1), geography and family size. Health status and gender are prohibited rating factors.", o:"11.9", ut:false},
    {q:"Which of the following is NOT one of the ACA's essential health benefits?", c:["Maternity and newborn care","Pediatric dental and vision care","Adult cosmetic surgery","Mental health and substance use disorder services"], a:2, w:"The ten EHB categories include maternity, pediatric oral and vision, and mental health/substance use, among others. Cosmetic surgery isn't an essential health benefit.", o:"11.9", ut:false}
